  "schema:identifier": "id-0e72f62ba23e4850881657e1d940212b",
  "schema:name": "Medium-term expenditure projections produced. ",
  "schema:description": "These are three-to-five-year financial forecasts that estimate the future costs of health services, workforce, and infrastructure. They provide a strategic outlook that extends beyond the immediate annual budget cycle to support long-term planning.\r\n\r\nThey allow for sustainable fiscal planning and the early identification of future funding requirements. This forward-looking approach helps prevent sudden budgetary shocks and supports the planning of large-scale national health initiatives.\r\n\r\nExample: A five-year projection showing the expected long-term costs of sustaining a new universal primary healthcare rollout.",
  "schema:category": "Motivation",
  "dcterms:isPartOf": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/archimate/0.2.0-draft.2.jsonld"
}
